-- title:
--   Gauss branches over the Γ₀(M') floor, case q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'\ge 1$ be an integer with $q\nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$, together with the hypothesis that some ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ sends $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$. Inside $L$-Laurent series, let $K$ be the intermediate field obtained by adjoining to $L$ the coefficientwise images of the rational $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, where $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, that field being the $\mathbb{Q}$-field generated by ratios $f/g$ of $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ having integral $q$-expansions; let $K_0$ be the analogous base change of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(M')$, assumed contained in $K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$. Let $W_0\subseteq K$ and $O_0\subseteq K_0$ be valuation subrings characterised by the Gauss condition: $f$ belongs to the ring exactly when $f\cdot y=x$ for some power series $x,y\in A[[T]]$ whose second factor has nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Then, $K$ being a $K_0$-algebra via the inclusion, for every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ fixing $K_0$ pointwise the valuation subring $\tau^{-1}(W_0)$ of $K$ satisfies: an element of $K_0$ lies in $\tau^{-1}(W_0)$ if and only if it lies in $O_0$; the resulting ring homomorphism $O_0\to\tau^{-1}(W_0)$ is local; and the extension of residue fields $\mathrm{ResidueField}(\tau^{-1}(W_0))/\mathrm{ResidueField}(O_0)$ is separable.
--
--   This is the $q=3$ case of the statement that the branches cut out by the Gauss valuation on the $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$-level function field lie above the Gauss point of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-level field with local inclusion and separable residue extension; at $q=3$ the relevant Igusa-type covering of the cusp branch is degree one, so several clauses hold for trivial reasons. It feeds the statement on comparison of valuation rings, ramification index one and separability for the $\Gamma_0(M')$-by-$X_H$ tower at $q=3$.
